' ============================================================ ' HomeSceneFocus.brs ' Manual focus/key routing between the left nav rail and the ' content rows. Roku's RowList handles up/down/left/right ' internally *within itself*, but moving focus OUT to the nav ' rail (and back) has to be done by hand. ' ============================================================ function onKeyEvent(key as string, press as boolean) as boolean if not press then return false handled = false if m.focusZone = "rows" if key = "left" ' Only hand off to nav if the RowList is already at its ' leftmost item -- RowList itself won't tell us this ' directly, so track the current column ourselves via ' rowItemFocused's itemIndex in onRowItemFocused (HomeScene.brs) if m.currentItemIndex = invalid or m.currentItemIndex = 0 m.focusZone = "nav" m.navRail.setFocus(true) handled = true end if end if else if m.focusZone = "nav" if key = "right" m.focusZone = "rows" m.contentRows.setFocus(true) handled = true else if key = "OK" ' Let NavRail's own onKeyEvent handle selection; ' just don't fall through and treat it as scene-level. handled = false end if end if return handled end function